<in reference to NunYaBidness' entire post>

While you may have some good points, you really need to work on your 
approach. Getting ticked off and yelling, screaming, and insulting is 
not going to help your cause.

Robbie did indeed abuse the english language (with the boycott comment), 
but he was correct when he said that people prefer "action games with no 
content." Look at the sales of Doom3. Very little content whatsoever. 
The plot is thin, the level design is poor, and people still buy it so 
they can blow demons back to Hell.

 From this it follows that people are no longer particularly interested 
in indepth gameplay, en masse. I personally believe it's because they 
want fast fun, and don't want to have to learn the idiosyncrasies of 
their game before they can get a whole lot of enjoyment out of it. 
Nethack is a perfect example. It's enjoyable until you accidently find 
Medusa's Lair (without having a clue that she existed). You come back 
wiser next time, but it wasn't the relaxing time you had envisioned when 
you first sat down (I use the pronoun 'you' to refer to the average 
gamer today).

You also seem to have forgotten everything you learned in Business 
class. EVERYTHING is about the market. Programmers don't OK projects. 
Level editors don't OK projects. Game balance technicians don't OK 
projects. The Financial Department OKs projects. And the Financial 
Department doesn't OK projects that cost $10 million to produce, and 
will only make $3 million because they only appeal to a small strata of 
gamers.

On a (somewhat) political note, both schools, and parents are "broken". 
Schools teach self-esteem, rather than math and reading, and parents 
grew up being taught self-esteem (rather than math and reading) and are 
now just as stupid as their kids are.

Windows 2K is not faster than any previous version of Windows. It may be 
faster, however (never benchmarked it). That said, it is far from 
"smaller, faster, and more reliable than Linux". I've seen people fit 
Linux on a machine with 4MB of memory. Please let me know when you do 
that with Windows 2K. Also, have you ever noticed that none of the 
supercomputers run Windows? As for more reliable, one only has to glance 
at the tech news headlines concerning viruses to know that that's not 
quite true.

And I'm sorry, but an Operating System (Windows Vista) that requires 
higher system specs (processor, memory, not sure on video card) than 
Doom3 is simply bloated.

In conclusion, you should probably avoid generalizing about people, and 
calling them names.


